  "reason": "The completed experiments show that RNA-only single-profile PCA is much stronger than image-only ResNet, with validation accuracy 0.4849 vs 0.2079 and F1 0.4639 vs 0.1718, so RNA is the more promising unimodal direction. However, there is still no evidence on whether multiprofile modeling and aggregation improve over the single-profile baseline. config_002 keeps the same RNA modality and PCA encoder as config_001 while adding multiprofile with the simplest aggregation, avgpool, so it isolates the profile/aggregation effect with minimal confounds. This is the best next experiment because it tests a central design decision, provides a baseline for comparing transformer aggregation later, and helps determine whether further budget should be spent on multiprofile or multimodal configurations."
}

